# ZenRayShards refactor — 2026-07-11

Full refactor of the ZenRayShards subsystem (upload scripts + pipeline libs + client read path),
running IN PARALLEL with a live 76 GB upload. This document is the contract: what is frozen, what
is safe, in what order things happen. Written to disk BEFORE any edit (context-loss insurance).

## Live constraint — the wrapper re-reads files from disk

`~/.zr-runs/dji-upload-10-07-et-07-07.sh` (nohup zsh, running) executes 4 sequential `node`
invocations. Step 1 (images, in RAM) is immune to disk edits; steps 2/3/4 spawn FRESH node
processes that load whatever is on disk at that moment. A mid-refactor file loaded by step 3
(333 images, NO relaunch-skip → duplicate tiles) or step 4 (53 GB video) is the nightmare case.

