| Repo naming `zenrayshards-<type>-<hex12>`, NEW repo per batch, zero remote checks | upload-vidraw-list.mjs:57, upload-img-list.mjs:24 | 313 repos renamed 2026-07-06; old names live on GitHub redirects — never recreate |
| `zenrayshards-img-*` = PUBLIC (jsDelivr), everything else PRIVATE (api.github.com + token) | img-ingest.mjs:16, naming convention | Visibility by name convention — the whole read path depends on it |
| Image chunking ≤19 MB, `cdnChunks[]` ALWAYS an array (even 1 element) | img-pipeline.mjs:88 `CHUNK_BYTES = 19*1024*1024` | jsDelivr refuses >~20 MB; uniform logic, no per-size special case |
| Deterministic IV (blob dedup) + AES-256-GCM, master key `.zenray-media-key` — never regenerate | img-pipeline.mjs, video-raw-lib.mjs:18 | IV change silently doubles storage; key regen = all past media unreadable |
| Video shard cap 4.0 GiB, LOCAL counter only, anticipated rollover | video-raw-lib.mjs:28 | GitHub soft limit 5 GB; asking GitHub for sizes was the "infinite reclone" bug |
| Incremental push every 900 MB (video, raised from 400 MB) / 900 MB (image, raised from 800 MB) — 2026-07-11, BOTH strictly under the empirically-proven <1 GB/push safety line (a bigger single push HANGS, no timeout catches it) | video-raw-lib.mjs:201 (~line, post-edit), img-ingest.mjs:170 | Anti-hang + no monolithic multi-GB pushes. Matthieu proposed 1900 MB assuming a 2000 MB GitHub limit — no such limit exists in this project or GitHub's docs; the real, tested ceiling here is <1 GB, corrected instead of applied blindly |
| Image manifests commit to zenray-data in ~900 MB BATCHES (2026-07-12, Matthieu's speed reversal): ingest N images → one `ctx.flush()` → resolve ALL → one grouped `pushBlobs` → one jsDelivr verify per (repo,commit). `ZR_IMG_BATCH_MB` tunes it (default 900; 0 = per-image = old media-by-media, same code path) | upload-img-list.mjs `flushBatch()` (patterned on upload-img-all.mjs) | ~480 images: ~4-5 shard pushes + ~5 zenray-data commits instead of ~480 each. Trade-off (accepted, reverses the 07-11 per-image request): images appear in Create per-batch, not one-by-one; a crash loses ≤1 batch (≤900 MB re-ingested next run, orphan binaries in a fresh shard, NEVER a duplicate tile — manifest path is deterministic) |
| All chunks of ONE image land in the SAME repo/commit | img-ingest.mjs:157 reserve() | A rollover between two chunks would break reconstruction |
| Manifest schema unchanged: new = `cdnChunks[]`+`cdnCommit`, old = `cdnPath` (pre-2026-07-07, never migrated) | resolveImgManifest, client useResolvedFull | Client must read BOTH forever |
| Video manifests pin raw.github URLs on commit SHA | video-raw-lib.mjs:269-271 | Unpinned URLs break on force-push/rollover |

